From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lite3-zig <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 07:17:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Allow disabling prefetching with
 LITE3_DISABLE_PREFETCHING

Prefetch hints may fault on non-x86 targets and read past the end of
kv_ofs[]; builds need a way to turn them off without editing the header.
---
 include/lite3.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/lite3.h b/include/lite3.h
index ba96219..056e0e0 100644
--- a/include/lite3.h
+++ b/include/lite3.h
@@ -180,8 +180,12 @@ Enabled by default.
 This *may* happen when:
 1. reading near unallocated page boundaries
 2. untrusted messages contain invalid offsets
+
+Define `LITE3_DISABLE_PREFETCHING` to turn it off without editing this header.
 */
+#ifndef LITE3_DISABLE_PREFETCHING
 #define LITE3_PREFETCHING
+#endif
 
 #if defined(DOXYGEN_ONLY) && !defined(LITE3_PREFETCHING)
 #define LITE3_PREFETCHING
